roadmap-doc: ./SPRINT-ROADMAP.md

###############################################################################
# MACHINE RULES FOR AGENTS
###############################################################################

agent-rules:

  # ── TARGET STRUCTURE (decided with Denis 2026-08-20) ─────────────────────────
  # ENDGAME: work-control is upstreamed by PR into app-agent-io/core as a BASE APP —
  # a peer of control/, not a resident of apps/. Not this stage, but shape code for it.
  # The upstream base-app pattern, verified in core/control/nuxt.config.ts:
  #     core/<name>/   = the LAYER — all infrastructure (server, pages, components)
  #     <name>/        = a THIN app — `extends ../core/<name>`, sets devServer.port,
  #                      holds branding overrides + public/ only
  # So the target split is  core/work-control/  +  work-control/  (port 3003).
  # WHY IT MATTERS BEYOND TIDINESS: today work-control is BOTH the orchestrator AND an
  # app inside apps/, and the code conflates the two — DEFAULT_TARGET_APP='work-control',
  # isProtectedBuildTarget guarding it by NAME, its own planning under apps/work-control/
  # planning/. That conflation is the root of the S41 defect where every proposed epic
  # defaulted to targetApp 'work-control' (the protected orchestrator) and Accept 422'd.
  # Once work-control leaves apps/, it stops being addressable as a build target
  # STRUCTURALLY, the name-based guard becomes redundant, and the bad default dissolves.
  # CONSTRAINT FOR NEW CODE: never hardcode `apps/work-control` as work-control's OWN
  # location. "Where customer apps live" (apps/) and "where work-control lives" are two
  # different facts that only coincide today.
  # PR HYGIENE: the fork carries things that must NEVER go upstream — untracked generated apps,
  # evidence/ folders, .env, demo seeds. The ~40 mock-generated sprints are GONE (S43-T11, commit
  # 8d8996c: 195 files, 7,410 deletions, ruling R4) with their provenance evidence preserved in
  # <planning-home>/CORPUS-PROVENANCE-EVIDENCE.md. T13 verified the PR diff against `main` — note
  # NO `upstream` remote is configured in the dev worktree, so the .pd's `git log upstream/main..`
  # step could not be run as written.
  - MANDATORY: every role loads INSTANCE.ti + APP-AGENT-PROTOCOL.md before any action (see §0 role matrix)
  - MCP preflight (intel/MCP-PREFLIGHT.ti) at session start; WARN user if :3000/mcp unreachable
  - Every new .ptl/.pd YAML MUST include protocol: ../APP-AGENT-PROTOCOL.md
  - PLANNER: every code .pd requires mcp/MCP.ti + templates/PD-APP-AGENT-BLOCK.md
  - Do NOT modify /core/ in customer forks — extend via organization + apps
  - Use MCP explain(slug) — do not preload ADRs; fallback to knowledge/*.md only when MCP offline (label [static fallback])
  - Load DEEP-FLOWS.md for request lifecycle orientation
  - Run bun run test (vitest) NOT bun test
  - Run feature:health after adding SEE annotations
  - Check PROBLEMS_REGISTER P0 before claiming repo is green (esp. P0-6 gitignore)
  - temp.md may contain secrets — never copy into Totem
  - Use bun --bun nuxt dev per app — turbo uses Node and breaks bun:sqlite
  # S05 additions
  - Agent-role taxonomy lives in organization/app/app.config.ts (agents block)
  - Per-app rules + gate semantics live in apps/work-control docs + work-control knowledge slug
  - Totem write-back: app writes .ptl/.pd at gate:LOCKED; human opens; agent then runs
  - Realtime via Nitro WebSocket (crossws), NOT Supabase Realtime
  - Persistence: Supabase via CORE_DATASOURCE_* (ADR-005 pattern); bun:sqlite dev fallback
  # S07 additions
  - Totem header rules live in docs/content/2.company/ + explain("organization-planning")
  - Organization layer does not auto-sync to knowledge or per-app docs
  # S08 additions
  - Default Accept target: apps/<targetApp>/planning/sprints/ (epic.targetApp, default work-control)
  - explain("in-repo-planning") for path resolver + env vars; legacy WORK_CONTROL_TOTEM_PATH fallback
  # S12 additions
  - Presence: in-memory registry + presence.sync on chat/board rooms; PresenceAvatars UI
  - usePresenceId() ephemeral tab UUID; agent auto-presence during task run
  # S36 + S41 additions (2026-08-20) — READ THESE FIRST, they override older entries
  - WORKTREE — FIXED 2026-08-20, do not "restore" the old values from memory: project.config.yml
      paths.code + paths.workspace now point at ../../../../app-agent-io/DAWWWB-app-agent-dev and
      repo.branch is `write-docs-in-auto`. That IS where the work is. The OTHER worktree
      (DAWWWB-app-agent, branch `vercel-demo`) is the parked Vercel demo. Still verify with
      `git branch --show-current` before trusting either file.
  - PLANNING HOME IS IN-REPO since S36: apps/work-control/planning/ (+ /sprints, /evidence).
      Do NOT author .ptl/.pd in this external totem instance; ../sprints/ is history only.
  - Sprint state: S36 CLOSED PARTIAL (2 DoD items still [~]); S41 CLOSED 2026-08-20 with T03
      OUTSTANDING. The chat->Accept->plan+docs half is PROVEN LIVE on apps/pulse-note.
      The daemon->OpenRouter build->boot->preview half HAS NEVER RUN. Treat every claim about
      it as unproven no matter how many green tests reference it.
  - S41 was NOT acceptance-first. Its charter said findings become LOCKED follow-ups, never
      inline fixes; Denis explicitly overrode that and S41-F01 was FIXED in-sprint. Do not
      repeat the override without an equally explicit human instruction.
  - PORT ALLOCATION AFTER S41-F01 (behaviour changed — old notes are wrong):
      * nextAppPort is no longer hard-capped at 3009. It walks 3002-3099, skipping RESERVED
        (3000/3001/3010-3014) and any port that is declared by another app OR held by a listener.
        It THROWS on exhaustion instead of silently colliding.
      * A port declared in package.json `scripts.dev` counts as declared, not just nuxt.config.ts.
      * boot-verify targets the app's OWN configured port via resolveBootPort — NOT the allocator.
      * An OCCUPIED port is now REFUSED before any spawn. This is correct but it is a NEW
        failure class: if Denis has the target app running, boot-verify fails loudly.
      * pulse-note / focus-timer / habit-tracker / kanban-board ALL still declare 3009.
      * A green boot needs a real proof: listener probe (three-valued, `unknown` proves nothing),
        child liveness (EADDRINUSE + on-exit), or the /api/health `app` identity marker.
  - GATE ANOMALY IS SETTLED — do not re-litigate. `gate: OPEN` at `status: PLANNED` on a .ptl is
      the fingerprint of a LEGITIMATE HUMAN open-gate, NOT a generator defect (10-for-10 against
      the historical activity log). No generator path can emit OPEN; openPtlGate() is the only
      writer and it rewrites the .ptl alone, which is why the .pd stay LOCKED.
      CAVEAT: that fingerprint applies to work-control-GENERATED artifacts only — hand-authored
      S41-F*/T* .pd at gate: OPEN are a separate, unrelated bookkeeping slip.
  - THE TWO FALSIFIED S41 CLAIMS ARE NOW CORRECTED, NOT MERELY ANNOTATED (S43-T12, 2026-08-24).
      The corrections live in S43-INVARIANTS.md §4 and that file is the ACTIVE invariants set:
      (1) the S38/S39 gate anomaly is a LEGITIMATE HUMAN open-gate whose tasks never ran — no
          generator path can emit `gate: OPEN`; planning-writer.ts:228's flip runs only through the
          human open-gate route, and it rewrites the .ptl alone (which is why the .pd stay LOCKED);
      (2) config reassignment is EFFECTIVE. resolveBootPort (runner/scaffold.ts:468) reads
          readConfiguredPort(appRoot) FIRST and only falls back to nextAppPort; loop.ts:444-455 calls
          it and supervise.ts:777 injects it as the supervisor's resolvePort. The old sentence
          described code that no longer exists, and the "only freeing the port helps" workaround it
          implied is obsolete.
  - INVARIANT #5 IS BROKEN ON DISK: 7 of 14 apps declare plain `nuxt dev` (no `bun --bun`),
      including pulse-note, which S41 itself scaffolded. The scaffolder emits the bad form while
      boot-verify spawns the good one, so a green boot never exercises the human start path.
  - Adversarial verification EARNS ITS COST: three lenses turned a green, tested S41-F01 fix into
      18 findings, one of which reproduced the original false green through the FIXED code path.
      Run it on anything load-bearing before calling it done.
  # test-count history — S41 close 62/687; follow-up 67/869; agent-honesty 70/1069; S43 open 78/1258
  - SUITE BASELINE 2026-08-24 at S43 close — `bun run test` = 98 files / 1731 tests, exit 0.
      `bun run typecheck` in apps/work-control exits 0.
      `bun run feature:health` now exits 1 on TWO broken refs, and the count moved for a reason worth
      knowing: core/docs/knowledge/work-control.md (long-standing, the slug is app-local by design)
      AND core/docs/knowledge/trig-calculator.md — created by the product WORKING. The daemon-built
      app followed the `// SEE: feature "slug" at <app-local path>` convention correctly, and
      core/cli/feature-health.js:23 resolves slugs against core/docs/knowledge/ only. So every app
      the daemon builds adds one broken ref. Filed as S43-F07. The layer-aware scanner that fixes it
      exists ONLY on pr/work-control-base-app and additionally needs `slug:` frontmatter the build
      agent does not emit. Do NOT "fix" an app-local slug by creating core/docs/knowledge/<slug>.md —
      in the resolver that file SHADOWS the layer's own, silently.
  - MCP WAS UP FOR THE S43 CLOSE (2026-08-24) — the first time in this chain that protocol §7's
      "MCP was up for verify" box is answered yes rather than gapped. Verified this session:
      GET / -> 200, GET /mcp -> 406, POST /mcp tools/list -> live tool list, explain("work-control")
      -> the correct app-agent description, census() -> 23 features. The S41-era squatter is gone.
      The standing rule is unchanged: PROBE :3000 before trusting explain(); label fallbacks
      [static fallback]. Being up today is not a property of the system, it is an observation.
  # AGENT-HONESTY BATCH additions (2026-08-20) — READ THESE BEFORE BELIEVING ANY "AI DID THIS" CLAIM
  - SUPERSEDED 2026-08-24 (S43-T12). This rule read "THE PRODUCT HAS NEVER BEEN OBSERVED DOING AI
      PLANNING." That was TRUE for everything written before 2026-08-24 and is FALSE now — do not
      keep repeating it, and do not delete the history it records either. Both halves:
      (a) STILL TRUE, and it is the whole reason this instance distrusts its own record: both
          pre-S43 "live" Accept runs (pulse-note 2026-07-11, quote-wall 2026-08-20) were served by
          the DETERMINISTIC MOCK agents, as was the ENTIRE generated corpus — 39 for 39 on
          planner.mock.ts's verbatim "Freeze the approach, data shapes, and contracts for ...",
          with root.mock.ts's canned epic titles ("Add authentication", "Build the API & data
          model", "Design the UI") on the boards. That corpus was deleted under ruling R4
          (S43-T11); the fingerprint evidence is preserved at
          <planning-home>/CORPUS-PROVENANCE-EVIDENCE.md.
      (b) NO LONGER TRUE as of 2026-08-24: apps/app2 was decomposed and built by the real Claude
          CLI after a human opened the gate. The output is model-authored on evidence, not on
          assertion — the generated source carries `// SEE: feature "trig-calculator" at
          apps/app2/docs/trig-module-design.md` (a repo convention nobody templated for it) and the
          QA doc records task-specific numeric verification. planner.mock.ts's fingerprint sentence
          appears nowhere in it.
      Infrastructure claims (ports, gate, datasource, daemon count, generator fidelity) were never
      affected by either half — they do not depend on who wrote the text.
  - WHY IT WAS INVISIBLE (S41-F13, fixed) — the OpenRouter account returned HTTP 402 Insufficient
      credits and ALL FOUR llm agents swallowed it with a bare `catch` and returned mock output,
      while /api/preflight said the ai-provider row was ok, wc_agents.kind said 'llm', and the UI
      result as AI work. Three assertions, all false, zero signal.
  - THE RULE THAT REPLACED IT — THE MOCK MAY SERVE, IT MAY NOT CLAIM. Every fallback goes through
      apps/work-control/server/agents/llm/degradation.ts `withProviderFallback(seam, primary,
      fallback, {scope})`, which serves the mock AND records a classified, redacted degradation.
      If you add a new agent or a new "... with AI" action, ROUTE IT THROUGH THAT SEAM. Never write
      `catch { return mock(...) }`, and never swap an empty result for the mock silently — that
      is the same lie, quieter (it was live in enrich/refactor/refactor-tasks and is now fixed).
  - wc_agents.kind IS NOT PROVENANCE for anything written before 2026-08-20. `resolveAgentKind()`
      decides from env PRESENCE, before the call, and never revises. A row reading 'mock' is a
      trustworthy upper bound; a row reading 'llm' proves NOTHING. New writes go through
      `effectiveAgentKind()` and are corrected in both directions; the six 'llm' rows from the live
      run are still wrong on disk and were deliberately not rewritten.
  - PROVIDER SITUATION — REWRITTEN 2026-08-24 (S43-T12). THE 2026-08-20 ENTRY IS DEAD; do not act
      on any memory of it. OpenRouter being out of credit (HTTP 402) is no longer on any default
      path, and the :8787 shim DOES NOT EXIST — ruling R3 (Denis, 2026-08-22) rejected the entire
      shim lineage outright and scripts/claude-provider.ts was DELETED (tombstone:
      <code>/apps/work-control/docs/agent-runtime.md:80-87). Do not resurrect it; do not point
      AI_PROVIDER_URL at it.
      CURRENT TRUTH: WORK_CONTROL_EXECUTOR=claude-cli, WORK_CONTROL_EFFORT=high (-> Opus). The CLI
      authenticates by SUBSCRIPTION OAuth out of $HOME — AI_PROVIDER_* is not read by any role in
      this configuration. executors/openrouter.ts is KEPT but demoted: legacy, deploy-only,
      non-default — still the only builder where no `claude` binary exists.
      THE HONESTY CAVEAT SURVIVES, unchanged and still load-bearing: preflight's ai-provider row is
      per-PROCESS, empty after a restart, and NEVER covers the separate `bun run runner` daemon.
      A green row is not proof that this run did AI work.
  - S41-F12 (fixed) — proposed epics used to default their targetApp to 'work-control', the PROTECTED
      orchestrator — so the flagship "describe it -> watch it build" path dead-ended by default, and
      NOT with a clean 422 — because apps/work-control/planning/sprints exists, the plan was written
      into the orchestrator's OWN corpus and the build was skipped as `blocked`. Now resolved from
      the conversation by server/agents/target-app.ts, with an honest self-announcing fallback.
      The derivation is ENGLISH-ONLY — a Russian-language request still resolves to the fallback.
  - RUN ADVERSARIAL VERIFICATION ON ANYTHING LOAD-BEARING. It paid again — three lenses turned this
      batch's green, tested fixes into 21 findings, including (a) retried 429/5xx being structurally
      unreachable because the ai SDK's RetryError carries no status code, and (b) a false-degradation
      "cry wolf" that labelled a genuinely successful run as mock. A wrong honesty badge is worse
      than no badge — it teaches the operator to ignore it.
  # SDEMO-B additions (2026-06-22) — PARKED branch, superseded by the in-repo S36/S41 chain
  - Two git worktrees: DAWWWB-app-agent (vercel-demo) + DAWWWB-app-agent-dev (test-app)
  - vercel-demo branch: preset:vercel, no hub:db, MemoryWorkControlRepo with seed, useRealtime stub
  - demoMode flag (NUXT_PUBLIC_DEMO_MODE=true): stubs WS + presence, fires mock task.moved after 3s
  - Vite SSR externalization bug fixed: inline chatRoom/boardRoom in client composables
  - vercel.json at monorepo root pointing to apps/work-control/.vercel/output

